### ==============================================================================
### SECURE NOTE-TAKING APPLICATION REST API TEST WORKBOOK
### Compatible with: VS Code REST Client extension, JetBrains HTTP Client, or curl
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@contentType = application/json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. AUTHENTICATION & ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL (RBAC)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Login as Default Administrator (Seeded automatically from .env)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@notetaking.local",
  "password": "AdminSecurePassword123!"
}

### Capture Admin Token
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.data.access_token}}

### 1.2 Privilege Escalation Defense: Attempt to self-register as Admin
# EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request (forbidNonWhitelisted rejects "role" field)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "attacker@example.com",
  "password": "AttackerPass123!",
  "name": "Malicious User",
  "role": "admin",
  "interests": ["hacking"]
}

### 1.3 Register Regular User A
# @name registerUserA
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "AlicePassword123!",
  "name": "Alice Developer",
  "interests": ["chess", "reading", "backend"]
}

### 1.4 Register Regular User B
# @name registerUserB
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "BobPassword123!",
  "name": "Bob Designer",
  "interests": ["chess", "art", "music"]
}

### 1.5 Login as User A
# @name loginUserA
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "AlicePassword123!"
}

### Capture User A Variables
@userAToken = {{loginUserA.response.body.data.access_token}}
@userAId = {{loginUserA.response.body.data.user.id}}

### 1.6 Login as User B
# @name loginUserB
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "bob@example.com",
  "password": "BobPassword123!"
}

### Capture User B Variables
@userBToken = {{loginUserB.response.body.data.access_token}}
@userBId = {{loginUserB.response.body.data.user.id}}

### 1.7 Get Current User Profile (User A)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. USERS MANAGEMENT & SCENARIO 1 AGGREGATION
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Scenario 1 Aggregation: Group Users by Interests
# PDF Constraint: Executed in exactly one collection.aggregate() call
# Supported by: UserSchema.index({ interests: 1 }) multikey index
# EXPECTED: Returns interest buckets (e.g. "chess" with both Alice and Bob)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/by-interests
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}

### 2.2 Admin List All Users (Paginated)
# PDF Requirement: Admin can list all users. Supported by createdAt_-1 index.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?page=1&limit=10&sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 2.3 Regular User Forbidden from Listing Users
# EXPECTED: 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}

### 2.4 Admin: Create User with Explicit Role
# PDF Requirement: Admin can add users
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "moderator@notetaking.local",
  "password": "ModPassword123!",
  "name": "Moderator Jane",
  "role": "admin",
  "interests": ["moderation", "security"]
}

### 2.5 User A: Update Self Profile (Interests)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Alice Senior Engineer",
  "interests": ["chess", "reading", "distributed-systems"]
}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. NOTES MODULE & STRICT OWNERSHIP ENFORCEMENT
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 User A: Create Note A1
# @name createNoteA1
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Alice Confidential Note 1",
  "content": "Secret system architecture notes."
}

### Capture Note A1 ID
@noteA1Id = {{createNoteA1.response.body.data.id}}

### 3.2 User A: Create Note A2
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Alice Project Roadmap",
  "content": "Q4 backend delivery timeline."
}

### 3.3 User B: Create Note B1
POST {{baseUrl}}/notes
Authorization: Bearer {{userBToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Bob UI Guidelines",
  "content": "Design system color tokens and typography."
}

### 3.4 User A: List Own Notes (Paginated)
# Supported by compound index: NoteSchema.index({ owner: 1, createdAt: -1 })
# EXPECTED: Returns ONLY Alice's notes (Note A1, Note A2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}

### 3.5 User B attempts to VIEW User A's Note
# EXPECTED: 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteA1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userBToken}}

### 3.6 User B attempts to EDIT User A's Note
# EXPECTED: 403 Forbidden
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteA1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userBToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Tampered Title by User B"
}

### 3.7 User B attempts to DELETE User A's Note
# EXPECTED: 403 Forbidden
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteA1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userBToken}}

### 3.8 Admin: View User A's Note
# PDF Requirement: Admin "Can view everyone's notes"
# EXPECTED: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteA1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3.9 Admin: Attempt to MODIFY User A's Note
# PDF Requirement: Admin can VIEW everyone's notes, but note edits strictly enforce ownership
# EXPECTED: 403 Forbidden
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteA1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Admin Override Attempt"
}

### 3.10 Admin: List All Notes Across All Users (Paginated)
# PDF Requirement: Admin can view everyone's notes. Supported by createdAt_-1 index.
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 3.11 User A: Successfully Update Own Note
# EXPECTED: 200 OK
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteA1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Alice Updated Confidential Note 1",
  "content": "Updated system design documentation."
}

### 3.12 User A: Successfully Delete Own Note
# EXPECTED: 200 OK
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/notes/{{noteA1Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. POSTS MODULE & SCENARIO 2 AGGREGATION ($lookup)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 User A: Create Post 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "MongoDB Indexing Strategies in Production",
  "content": "Why ESR (Equality, Sort, Range) rule eliminates in-memory sorts."
}

### 4.2 User A: Create Post 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/posts
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Clean Layered Architecture with NestJS",
  "content": "Separating DTOs, ViewModels, and Mongoose repositories."
}

### 4.3 Public Feed: List All Posts (Paginated)
# Open to all callers. Supported by PostSchema.index({ createdAt: -1 })
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts?page=1&limit=10

### 4.4 Scenario 2 Aggregation: Retrieve All Posts Belongs to User A ($lookup)
# PDF Constraint: Single aggregation pipeline with a $lookup stage
# Supported by: PostSchema.index({ author: 1, createdAt: -1 })
# EXPECTED: Returns Alice's posts with author details populated via $lookup
GET {{baseUrl}}/posts/user/{{userAId}}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. QUERY VALIDATION & PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATIONS
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5.1 Invalid ObjectId in Note Filter
# EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request ("owner must be a valid MongoDB ObjectId")
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes?owner=invalid-non-object-id
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 5.2 Disallowed Unindexed Sort Field
# PDF Constraint: Strict indexing efficiency; arbitrary in-memory sorts forbidden
# EXPECTED: 400 Bad Request ("sortBy must be an indexed field (createdAt)")
GET {{baseUrl}}/notes?sortBy=content
Authorization: Bearer {{userAToken}}
